.TH TOCSMITH 1 "September 13, 2026" "TocSmith 1.0 (346)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tocsmith \- forge navigable, finished PDFs from printed tables of contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tocsmith
.RI [ options ]
.I pdf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TocSmith
examines the extractable text layer of a PDF, locates likely table-of-contents
pages, resolves their entries to document headings, and can write a finished
copy with a nested sidebar outline.
.PP
When writing a PDF, TocSmith can also crop oversized pages when credible crop
marks identify the intended trim, normalize rotated pages, add a footer
watermark, and record its decisions in a text log. The input PDF is not
modified.
.PP
With no writing option, TocSmith performs analysis only and prints JSON to
standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the TocSmith release and build number and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-write-bookmarks
Write a new PDF with conservative sidebar bookmarks and page finishing.
Without an explicit output path, the destination is named by adding
.B .bookmarked
before the input filename extension.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " path"
Write the generated PDF to
.IR path .
Supplying this option implies
.BR \-\-write-bookmarks .
.TP
.BI \-\-min-match-score " score"
Set the minimum anchor confidence for root bookmark entries. The default is
0.85. Child entries beneath an accepted parent may use a slightly lower guarded
threshold.
.TP
.BI \-\-watermark " text"
Set the footer text written on generated pages. The default is
.BR TocSmith .
Pass an empty string to disable the footer.
.SH OUTPUT FILES
For an input named
.BR manual.pdf ,
the default writing mode creates:
.TP
.B manual.bookmarked.pdf
The finished PDF containing generated sidebar bookmarks.
.TP
.B manual.bookmarked.pdf.log.txt
A human-readable record of accepted and skipped TOC entries, match scores,
anchor pages, crop count, and watermark count.
.SH EXIT STATUS
TocSmith exits with status 0 after successful analysis or writing. A nonzero
status indicates invalid input, a missing dependency, a PDF without extractable
text when writing was requested, or an output failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Analyze a PDF and print JSON:
.PP
.EX
tocsmith manual.pdf
.EE
.PP
Create the default finished copy:
.PP
.EX
tocsmith manual.pdf --write-bookmarks
.EE
.PP
Choose the output and a private footer without storing that footer in source
control:
.PP
.EX
tocsmith manual.pdf --output finished.pdf --watermark "Archive copy"
.EE
.PP
Create a finished copy without a footer:
.PP
.EX
tocsmith manual.pdf --write-bookmarks --watermark ""
.EE
.SH NOTES
TocSmith requires an extractable text layer. Scan-only PDFs must be processed
with OCR before TocSmith can derive reliable headings and bookmarks.
.PP
TOC interpretation and anchor selection are heuristic. TocSmith deliberately
skips uncertain entries and writes a decision log for review.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1)
